# Text formatting: Highlight, a color behind a styled part of a line, like a highlighter.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Text formatting · Highlight
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: source
			Typography:
				Font: IBM Plex Mono
				Size: 9
				Color: muted
		For style: result
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 14 0
			Typography:
				Size: 13
				Line height: 18
				Markup: markdown
		For style: mark
			Typography:
				Highlight: #FFE680
		For style: alert
			Typography:
				Highlight: #B3261E
				Color: #FFFFFF
				Bold: true
	Section:
		Text: Text formatting
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Highlight
		Paragraph: `Highlight`, in the `For style` rule of a styled part (`[text]{name}`), paints a color behind it. On each line the part is on, it is a rectangle as wide as the part and as tall as the font of its box, with no padding; it does not change the line. The text is checked for contrast against it. In a box, the color behind it is its `Background`.
			Style: intro
		Text: Payment is due on [15 May]{mark}.
			Style: source
		Text: Payment is due on [15 May]{mark}.
			Style: result
		Text: A part that crosses lines is highlighted on each of them, without the space where the line breaks
			Style: label
		Text: The [walnut chair with a wool seat and a back of woven cane]{mark} is back in stock.
			Style: result
			Box:
				Width: 60mm
		Text: [OVERDUE]{alert} Invoice 2026-118, with [**bold**, ++underlined++ and ~~struck~~ text]{mark} inside.
			Style: source
		Text: [OVERDUE]{alert} Invoice 2026-118, with [**bold**, ++underlined++ and ~~struck~~ text]{mark} inside.
